  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# iiVolumetricSolidMesh\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiVolumetricSolidMesh"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "iiVolumetricSolidMesh is a Qt-free C++23 SDK for a hybrid 3D object: an\nimmutable CAD design snapshot, a derived tetrahedral volume and triangle\nsurface, and material particles representing non-overlapping tetrahedral cells. Applications can inspect the\nsurface as a mesh and use separate nodal or particle simulation states without\nmodifying the CAD source.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "The first native authoring and meshing path is a dimensioned box. Custom CAD\nkernels and tetrahedral meshers are attached through independent interfaces;\nno other iiSDK module is a dependency. Materials and their spatial regions\nare separate. Reference mass, center of mass, and centroidal inertia are\nintegrated over the piecewise-uniform tetrahedra, while particle inertia is\nreported separately as a point-mass approximation. A material-only snapshot\nupdate recalculates mass without remeshing or resampling the existing cells.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 17,
      "end_line": 21,
      "raw": "The SDK supplies FEM and particle-solver interfaces, not FEM, MPM, collision,\nfracture, or rendering solvers. General B-Rep/NURBS/CSG editing and arbitrary\nsolid tetrahedralization require application-supplied implementations. The\napplication is responsible for supplying a non-overlapping, conforming volume\nmesh and preserving or publishing files through its file provider.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 22,
      "end_line": 22,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 23,
      "end_line": 27,
      "raw": "```sh\ncmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 32,
      "raw": "Installation can be requested explicitly with `./install.sh` or an alternative\nprefix as its first argument. See the [architecture and contracts](docs/architecture.md)\nfor units, error handling, numerical assumptions, sample generation, solver\nboundaries, and the integration example.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 33,
      "end_line": 33,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
